<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime exceptions for the Veld Desktop app bundle's Developer ID
  signature (release builds only; local and pull-request builds are ad-hoc and
  carry no entitlements). `electron-builder.yml` names this file explicitly; the
  nested helpers and frameworks get the sibling `entitlements.mac.inherit.plist`.

  The hardened runtime is not optional here: notarization requires it.

  - allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8 compiles JavaScript at run
    time. Without them the app is signed, notarized, and crashes on launch.
  - disable-library-validation: not needed for Electron's own code (every nested
    framework is signed with our Team ID too). Kept because it is
    electron-builder's own default and removing it can only be validated by
    launching a Developer ID build; being wrong means a crash on launch for every
    user. Revisit once a signed build exists: drop it, launch, restore only if
    that fails.

  Deliberately absent: the App Sandbox (Developer ID, not Mac App Store), and
  allow-dyld-environment-variables — the app only spawns `veld` itself, and a
  GUI app launched from Finder never had the user's shell DYLD_* to pass on.

  Byte-for-byte the same keys as electron-builder's fallback template, committed
  anyway: a security property of the shipped binary belongs where a reviewer can
  see it, not in node_modules where a dependency bump can change it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
